// spec: EXP-003
//
// EXP-003 binds 'as' at the unary level, so this is '(A as Integer) > 3' and
// prints true.  'as' binds below the comparison instead: the cast consumes the
// whole expression and the comparison has nothing left to attach to.
//
// ⚠️ ONE FILE, because only the parse failure distinguishes the two readings
// today.  The other symptom -- 'True and A as Integer' casting the conjunction
// rather than A -- prints 5 under BOTH precedences, since a cast has no runtime
// effect [DEF-12] and 'and' yields an operand.  A defect case that records the
// same value the fixed behaviour would produce is evidence of nothing, so it is
// not kept here.
//
// ⚠️ That symptom becomes observable the moment DEF-12 is fixed: a checked cast
// covering the conjunction raises where one covering A does not.  Fixing DEF-12
// without this turns a latent oddity into a live fault.

var A : Any := 5;
WriteLn (A as Integer > 3);
